    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1178">

                <pb facs="0960" n="844" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg844"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/6953.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Admiral Winslow to the Secretary of the
                    Navy</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Flagship “San Diego</hi>,” <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">San Francisco</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 20, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>M–3104, <hi rendition="#italic">Raleigh</hi> from Guaymas reports: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>General Dieguez states that General Estrada with troops will arrive in
                            San Bias within three days.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>No adequate protection will be afforded these people by Mexican forces unless
                    great pressure can be brought to bear on General Dieguez by higher authorities,
                    which can only be brought about by our Government in Washington.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winslow.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
